{
  "title": "The aorist",
  "note": "The aorist views an action as a simple whole, usually in the past: ἔλυσα, 'I loosed'. First aorist: augment + stem + σα: ἔλυσα, ἔλυσας, ἔλυσε(ν), ἐλύσαμεν, ἐλύσατε, ἔλυσαν. Second aorists use a different stem with imperfect endings: λαμβάνω → ἔλαβον. In a compound the augment follows the prefix: ἀπο-θνῄσκω → ἀπέθανον. Aorist passive: ἐλύθην, 'I was loosed'.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Perseus Digital Library (Smyth, Greek Grammar: the aorist)",
    "u": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/"
  },
